-- title:
--   Level transport, G-label and Frobenius parity over a local base
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison package for fake elliptic curves, organised into the following groups of data and hypotheses.
--
--   *Arithmetic base.* Primes $r$, $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, a positive integer $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree; a discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ which is a domain of characteristic zero with uniformiser $\pi$ (irreducible), $\pi$-adically complete, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and with $(r) = (\pi)$; a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero. Further, a characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo it, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo it, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it; finally a homomorphism $vdet$ from $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) whose value $n$ at $g$ is characterised by $\det g$ being a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^{n}$.
--
--   *Quaternionic data and moduli.* Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $a>0$ or $b>0$ and the completions of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ at a finite place are division algebras exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$; a scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point map $pt$ making it a coarse moduli space `IsCoarseModuli` for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ data; an integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $ptF$ a fine moduli structure `IsFineModuli` for such curves with full level-$n$ structure; a group $G$ acting on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$, satisfying `IsLevelTwistAction` (the action is over the base, realises level twisting by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$); a morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$, invariant under $\rho$ and compatible with the point maps. Also a Hecke tower: for each prime $\ell \neq r,\bar r$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra level $\ell$, together with the two degeneracy maps $d_0, d_1$ to $\mathcal X$ over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1$ computing the $\ell$-isogenous curve; and two Atkin–Lehner endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base, realising `IsAtkinLehnerQuotient` at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points.
--
--   *Definite quaternion side.* Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt ... rbar` (so $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and ramification exactly above $\bar r$); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ inside it; a finite-adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that the meet order of $R_1$ and $n_1$ is Eichler of level $N r$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $2\times2$ matrices over $K_0$; a finite place $v$ above $r$; a subgroup $\Gamma t$ of the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ characterised as the away-from-$v$ unit group of $R_1$; Hecke elements $s_\ell$ and finite ideles $sf_\ell$ indexed by primes $\ell \neq r,\bar r$, subject to the local conditions `hs` (away from $r$ the local component of $sf_\ell$ is $s_\ell$, at $r$ it is $1$, the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set or prime Hecke set of the meet order according as $\ell \mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$); the congruence subgroups $\Gamma t_\ell = \Gamma t \cap s_\ell \Gamma t s_\ell^{-1}$; and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma t$.
--
--   *Order coordinates and the base-point curve.* The assumption $h\Lambda\mathbb Z$ that every integer lies in $\Lambda$; a coordinate map $coord$ on $\Lambda$ with `IsOrderCoord` (additive, unital, multiplicative in the twisted sense, injective, dense, and compatible with reduced traces) with values in pairs of Witt vectors $\mathrm{Zp2}\,r$. Over the residue ring $Onr/(\pi)$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ for $A_0$ of dimension $2$ realising $A_0$ as a formal module via $coord$ and $X_0$, and families $e, e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma t$, with $e\gamma$ over the base and degrees $\deg \gamma$.
--
--   *The uniformisation hypotheses* `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` and `hE5a`–`hE5e` (summarised here) assert, respectively: each $e\gamma,e'\gamma$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; that scalar $\gamma$ act by the corresponding integer up to powers of $r$; conversely that $e\gamma$ being an integer multiplication forces $\gamma$ scalar; that for any injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $2\times 2$ matrices over $K_0$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced, in the formal coordinates $\theta_0$, by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; that each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ is moved by $e\gamma$ by a label $lab(\gamma) \in \Lambda$, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$; that on an algebraically closed field every $r$-power isogeny preserving the level structure on a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; and, for an auxiliary order $R_2 \subseteq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂r`) and a family $\hat e$ on $R_2$, that $\hat e$ is additive, $\Lambda$-equivariant and level-preserving, is multiplicative and unital, sends integers to integer multiplication, satisfies $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = \mathrm{nrd}(x)$, agrees with $e\gamma$ for $x$ an $r$-power multiple of $\gamma$, and that the matrix description of `hE2` holds simultaneously for $\Gamma t$ and for $R_2$ with one and the same $g$.
--
--   *The formal moduli package.* A ring map $\iota : \mathrm{Zp2}\,r \to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for $\iota$ and of height $4$; a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf; a map $\eta$ sending rigidified objects to points of $MD$, with `hη` asserting (i) $\eta$ separates admissible rigidifications exactly up to isomorphism, (ii) naturality of $\eta$ under base change of admissible objects, and (iii) local liftability of every point of $MD$ to an admissible rigidification on a Zariski cover; and an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action and $\varpi$ of $\Phi$ into $2\times2$ matrices over $K_0$ whose image is, up to a fixed power $r^{m}$, exactly the matrices over $\mathcal O$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   *The Drinfeld comparison.* A family $eD$ of maps from the points of the functor $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,MD$ on $\pi$-nilpotent Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from $Onr$ and a Deligne datum for $(K_0,\pi)$, assumed natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), compatible with the leg on first components (`hfstD`), transforming the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), sending $\varpi$-translation to the Frobenius twist of the leg by $1$ with unchanged datum (`hPiD`), and such that $\varpi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`).
--
--   *Transport data.* A ring map $\kappa : Onr/(\pi) \to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps; a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ exhibiting an isogeny of height $4 n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$; a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on the reduction: a curve $A_{0w}$ with maps $aw$, $aw'$ realising `IsAtkinLehnerQuotientVia` at $\bar r$, and $bw$, $bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level, together with `hJOINTw`, asserting that the matrix description of `hE2` holds with one $g$ both for all $\gamma \in \Gamma t$ and for the composite $aw \text{ followed by } bw$, the latter matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to a power of $r$.
--
--   *The rigidified-to-$G$ map.* A map $\Xi$ assigning to each $\pi$-nilpotent Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, leg $\psi : Onr \to B$ and rigidified curve over $(B,\psi)$ a point of $\mathrm{GPoint}\,\mathcal O\,MD\,B$, subject to: `hΞleg`, over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $Fr^{k}$ of $\psi$ for some integer $k$; `hΞnat`, naturality under base change of rigidifications; `hΞiso`, invariance of $\Xi$ under isomorphism of rigidified curves in the stated sense; and `hΞdef`, over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, for every rigidified curve whose underlying curve is a formal module via $coord$, $X$ and $\theta$, there exist $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, realising the rigidity transport `IsRigTransport` of $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with parameter $j$, admissible for the leg $Fr^{-j}\psi$, and $\Xi$ of the curve equals the triple $(Fr^{-j}\psi, \eta(t))$. Additionally a fixed $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and the equivariance hypotheses `heqΓ` and `heqW`: translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ (respectively passing to the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, with the matching rigidification data and $\bar r$ invertible) makes $\Xi$ change by the action of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$ (respectively $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$) for some integer $c$, in the sense of `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy`.
--
--   *The point functor $PR$.* A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a leg $\chi_C : Onr \to C$, an algebra functor $PR$ on $C$-algebras and a point map $ptR$ defined on pairs (curve with full level $n$, rigidification) whose leg is induced from $\chi_C$; subject to naturality under $C$-algebra maps compatible with the level structure and the rigidification (`hR2`), surjectivity of $ptR$ (`hR3s`), injectivity up to level isomorphism and comparison of rigidifications over test algebras with connected spectrum (`hR3i`), and the converse implication (`hR1`).
--
--   Finally, let $S$ be a Noetherian local $C$-algebra with a compatible $\mathcal O$-structure in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\psi_S : Onr \to S$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $u = (E, P)$ a fake elliptic curve over $S$ with full level-$n$ structure, and $\varrho$ a rigidification of $E$ along $\psi_S$ relative to $A_0$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$, an element $g$ of $G$ and an index $j \in \{0,1\}$ such that: first, $P_n$ is the normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$ in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport` for the data $Fr$, $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$, $\Phi$, $\iota$, $coord$; second, the given level structure $P$ of $u$ is the push-forward of $P_n$ under the action of $\chi(g)$ on $E$; and third, the leg of $\Xi(S,\psi_S)(E,\varrho)$ equals the Frobenius twist $Fr^{-j}$ of $\psi_S$.
--
--   This is the local-base form of the labelling step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$: over a local base every full level-$n$ structure differs from the height-normalised transport of the fixed structure $P_0$ by a single $G$-label, and the leg of the associated point of the formal moduli functor is a Frobenius twist by $0$ or $1$. It is used in the proof that the point map $ptR$ detects equality of level data through the labels $\chi$.
